<title>TURKEY: Turk Netas 9-month profits up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Netas 9-month profits up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	2,176.03  vs  1,894.31</p>
<p>    Net profit			 2,714.39  vs  2,362.97</p>
<p>    Net sales			 10,781.58  vs  4,324.80</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 3,000.50  vs  1,001.33</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     1,646.96  vs  3,343.82</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		390.37  vs    439.07</p>
<p>    Interest paid			 27.59  vs    180.34</p>
<p>    Total debts			5,716.69  vs  3,586.94</p>
<p>    Equity			     7,713.54  vs  5,630.93</p>
<p>    Capital			    1,247.40  vs  1,247.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish telecommunications equipment producer Netas-Northern Electric Telekomunikasyon A.S. is owned 51.85 percent by Canada's Northern Telecom Int..</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875 EKS</p>
</text>
